\par
\b 1. Product Overview\b0\par
\par
\b Product Summary\b0\par
A Brunei-first personal finance app that helps users manage their monthly salary, expenses, debt obligations, and savings using a simple planning workflow, bank statement imports, and actionable insights.\par
\par
The product is inspired by the discipline of tools like YNAB, but simplified and localized for the Brunei market.\par
\par
\b Core Promise\b0\par
Help Brunei users understand where their money goes, plan their monthly finances clearly, and reduce financial stress.\par
\par
\b MVP Objective\b0\par
Build a usable subscription-ready MVP that validates:\par
- demand in the Brunei market\par
- local bank statement import usefulness\par
- recurring monthly engagement\par
- willingness to pay for clarity and planning\par
\par
\b 2. Problem Statement\b0\par
\par
Many Brunei users:\par
- receive a monthly salary\par
- have recurring commitments and debts\par
- do not track expenses consistently\par
- struggle to understand where their money goes\par
- lack a simple system to plan spending between paydays\par
\par
Existing budgeting apps are often:\par
- too generic\par
- too complicated\par
- not localized to Brunei banking and spending patterns\par
- unsupported for local bank statement formats\par
- not focused on debt planning and salary allocation\par
\par
There is an opportunity to create a simple, trusted, locally relevant finance app for Brunei users.\par
\par
\b 3. Product Vision\b0\par
\par
To become the go-to personal finance app for Brunei users by making money management simple, local, practical, and habit-forming.\par
\par
\b 4. Target Users\b0\par
\par
\b Primary Segment\b0\par
Brunei-based salaried professionals aged 23–40 who:\par
- receive fixed monthly income\par
- use BIBD and/or Baiduri\par
- have debts or recurring commitments\par
- want better control over monthly spending\par
- are comfortable using mobile/web apps\par
- are not currently using advanced budgeting software\par
\par
\b Secondary Segment\b0\par
Young married couples and households who want:\par
- better spending control\par
- debt visibility\par
- savings planning\par
- a clearer monthly money system\par
\par
\b User Characteristics\b0\par
- wants clarity, not complexity\par
- values convenience\par
- may currently use spreadsheets, notes, or nothing\par
- wants practical guidance, not finance jargon\par
- may feel stress around payday-to-payday cash flow\par
\par
\b 5. Jobs To Be Done\b0\par
\par
Users hire this app to:\par
- understand where their salary goes every month\par
- track spending without too much manual effort\par
- import transaction history from local bank statements\par
- manage debt obligations clearly\par
- decide how much they can spend safely\par
- plan savings and commitments before overspending happens\par
- get simple monthly financial insights\par
\par
\b 6. Product Positioning\b0\par
\par
\b Positioning Statement\b0\par
For Brunei salary earners who want control over their money, this app is a local-first personal finance planner that turns salary, statements, spending, and debt into a clear monthly plan.\par
\par
\b Differentiators\b0\par
- Brunei-local focus\par
- BIBD and Baiduri statement support\par
- salary-to-payday planning\par
- debt payoff support\par
- simpler than traditional budgeting tools\par
- built around practical monthly use, not finance complexity\par
\par
\b 7. MVP Scope\b0\par
\par
\b In Scope for MVP\b0\par
\par
\b 7.1 Account & Authentication\b0\par
- user registration\par
- login/logout\par
- password reset\par
- profile management\par
\par
\b 7.2 Onboarding\b0\par
- set monthly salary\par
- set payday\par
- choose default budgeting categories\par
- add fixed monthly commitments\par
- add debts/loans\par
\par
\b 7.3 Dashboard\b0\par
- monthly income\par
- committed amount\par
- amount spent\par
- amount remaining\par
- debt summary\par
- top spending categories\par
- simple financial insights\par
\par
\b 7.4 Expense Tracking\b0\par
- add manual transactions\par
- edit/delete transactions\par
- categorize expenses\par
- filter by date/category/account\par
- monthly expense summaries\par
\par
\b 7.5 Monthly Budget / Plan\b0\par
- allocate monthly salary into categories\par
- compare planned vs actual\par
- track remaining budget by category\par
- show total unallocated or remaining amount\par
\par
\b 7.6 Debt Planner\b0\par
- add debt items\par
- set balance, monthly payment, and rate (optional)\par
- view estimated payoff timeline\par
- simulate extra monthly payment\par
- calculate total monthly debt burden\par
\par
\b 7.7 Bank Statement Import\b0\par
Initial support:\par
- BIBD PDF statement import\par
- Baiduri PDF statement import\par
\par
Flow:\par
- user uploads statement PDF\par
- app parses transactions\par
- user reviews parsed rows\par
- user confirms import\par
- app stores transactions in account history\par
\par
\b 7.8 Insights\b0\par
Rules-based financial insights such as:\par
- top spending category\par
- debt-to-income ratio\par
- overspending alerts\par
- spending trend from prior month\par
- remaining money before payday\par
- budget variance by category\par
\par
\b 7.9 Subscription Readiness\b0\par
- free vs premium feature gating\par
- premium screen/paywall placeholder\par
- billing integration can be basic in MVP, but architecture should support subscription plans\par
\par
\b Out of Scope for MVP\b0\par
- direct bank account login integration\par
- open banking connections\par
- investment tracking\par
- stock/crypto portfolio features\par
- family/shared budgeting\par
- bill payment\par
- loan applications\par
- financial marketplace features\par
- advanced AI assistant/chat\par
- full receipt OCR\par
- tax/accounting modules\par
- multi-country support\par
\par
\b 8. Key User Flows\b0\par
\par
\b Flow 1: New User Onboarding\b0\par
1. User signs up\par
2. User enters monthly salary\par
3. User sets payday\par
4. User adds fixed monthly commitments\par
5. User adds debt items\par
6. User chooses or confirms categories\par
7. User lands on dashboard with initial monthly plan\par
\par
\b Flow 2: Manual Expense Tracking\b0\par
1. User clicks add transaction\par
2. User enters amount, date, merchant, category\par
3. Transaction is saved\par
4. Dashboard and budget figures update\par
\par
\b Flow 3: Bank Statement Import\b0\par
1. User opens statement import\par
2. User selects bank and uploads PDF\par
3. App parses transactions\par
4. User reviews extracted rows\par
5. User edits categories/errors if needed\par
6. User confirms import\par
7. Transactions are added to the ledger\par
\par
\b Flow 4: Debt Management\b0\par
1. User adds debt item\par
2. User sees total debt summary\par
3. User enters extra payment scenario\par
4. App recalculates payoff estimate\par
5. User sees debt improvement outcome\par
\par
\b Flow 5: Monthly Review\b0\par
1. User opens dashboard near payday or month-end\par
2. User reviews spending vs plan\par
3. User checks debt status\par
4. User sees financial insights\par
5. User adjusts next month’s plan\par
\par
\b 9. Functional Requirements\b0\par
\par
\b 9.1 Authentication\b0\par
The system must:\par
- allow users to register with email/password\par
- allow secure login/logout\par
- support password reset\par
- protect private user data by account ownership\par
\par
\b 9.2 User Profile\b0\par
The system must store:\par
- full name\par
- email\par
- default currency (BND)\par
- payday\par
- monthly income\par
- preferred categories\par
\par
\b 9.3 Commitments\b0\par
The system must allow users to add recurring monthly commitments:\par
- rent\par
- utility bills\par
- family support\par
- subscriptions\par
- insurance/takaful\par
- school fees\par
- others\par
\par
Fields:\par
- label\par
- amount\par
- due date (optional)\par
- recurrence (monthly by default)\par
\par
\b 9.4 Transactions\b0\par
The system must allow:\par
- manual transaction creation\par
- import-based transaction creation\par
- editing/deleting transactions\par
- transaction categorization\par
\par
Transaction fields:\par
- date\par
- amount\par
- type (debit/credit)\par
- merchant/description\par
- category\par
- account\par
- source\par
- notes\par
\par
\b 9.5 Categories\b0\par
The system must:\par
- provide starter categories\par
- allow category assignment\par
- support category-level budget comparison\par
\par
Suggested starter categories:\par
- groceries\par
- dining\par
- transport\par
- fuel\par
- shopping\par
- utilities\par
- phone/internet\par
- debt repayment\par
- savings\par
- family support\par
- insurance/takaful\par
- education\par
- health\par
- entertainment\par
- others\par
\par
\b 9.6 Monthly Budgeting\b0\par
The system must:\par
- allow budget allocation by category for a given month\par
- compare actual spending against plan\par
- calculate remaining amount\par
- display category-level and overall variance\par
\par
\b 9.7 Debt Planner\b0\par
The system must:\par
- allow multiple debts per user\par
- store debt type, lender, balance, monthly payment, and interest/profit rate if provided\par
- calculate debt-to-income burden\par
- provide simple payoff estimates\par
- simulate extra monthly payment scenarios\par
\par
\b 9.8 Statement Import\b0\par
The system must:\par
- accept supported PDF files\par
- identify bank/source format\par
- parse rows into normalized transaction records\par
- flag uncertain rows\par
- require user review before final import\par
- prevent duplicate import if possible\par
\par
\b 9.9 Insights\b0\par
The system must generate simple rules-based insights such as:\par
- top category this month\par
- increase/decrease by category vs previous month\par
- debt load ratio\par
- projected remaining spend before payday\par
- warning when total commitments exceed configurable thresholds\par
\par
\b 9.10 Subscription Gating\b0\par
The system should support:\par
- free users with limited access\par
- premium users with statement import and advanced planning features\par
- subscription flags at user level\par
\par
\b 10. Non-Functional Requirements\b0\par
\par
\b Performance\b0\par
- dashboard should load quickly for normal monthly transaction volumes\par
- statement upload parsing should complete within a reasonable time\par
- app should handle several hundred to a few thousand transactions per user\par
\par
\b Security\b0\par
- all user data must be private\par
- all file uploads must be access-controlled\par
- passwords must be securely managed by auth provider\par
- sensitive finance documents must not be publicly exposed\par
- imported data must be tied only to the uploading user\par
\par
\b Reliability\b0\par
- statement imports should fail gracefully\par
- invalid files should return clear error messages\par
- calculations should be deterministic and testable\par
\par
\b Usability\b0\par
- onboarding should be simple and guided\par
- language should be plain and non-technical\par
- key numbers should be immediately visible\par
- app should feel less like accounting software and more like a practical planning tool\par
\par
\b 11. UX Principles\b0\par
- Simple first - do not overwhelm users\par
- Trust before cleverness - accuracy and clarity matter more than flashy AI\par
- Monthly planning mindset - design around payday and monthly cycles\par
- Local relevance - categories, language, and logic should fit Brunei users\par
- Review before import - user must always be able to verify imported statement data\par
\par
