\b 18. Risks and Mitigations\b0\par
\par
\b Risk: statement parsing errors\b0\par
\b Mitigation:\b0\par
- start with only BIBD and Baiduri\par
- always require review before import\par
- collect real sample statements for testing\par
- build parser by bank template, not generic logic\par
\par
\b Risk: users lose interest after first use\b0\par
\b Mitigation:\b0\par
- build around monthly payday workflow\par
- focus dashboard on how much is left\par
- provide practical monthly insights\par
\par
\b Risk: product feels too complicated\b0\par
\b Mitigation:\b0\par
- guide onboarding\par
- reduce jargon\par
- keep screens focused\par
- avoid too many setup fields initially\par
\par
\b Risk: low willingness to pay\b0\par
\b Mitigation:\b0\par
- reserve high-value convenience features for premium\par
- test pricing early with interview users\par
- keep free tier useful but limited\par
\par
\b Risk: trust/security concerns\b0\par
\b Mitigation:\b0\par
- no direct bank credentials in MVP\par
- private file storage\par
- explicit privacy messaging\par
- clear user control over imports\par
\par
